nce we ought to be able to\nobtain the same result by putting $n+1$ for $n$ in the expression\nfor $V_{n}$ and multiplying by $n+1$, we obtain the following equa-\ntions,\n$$(n+1) A_{n+1 \\cdot s}=(2 n-28+1) A_{n \\cdot s}=-A_{n \\cdot s-1} .$$\n(39)\nIf we put $s=0$, we obtain\n$$(n+1) A_{n+1 \\cdot 0}=(2 n+1) A_{n \\cdot 0} ;$$\n(40)\nand therefore, since $A_{1 \\cdot 0}=1$,\n$$A_{n, 0}=\\frac{2 n!}{2^{n}(n!)^{2}}$$\n(41)\nand from this we obtain the general value of the coefficient\n$$A_{n, s}=(-1)^{\\cdot} \\frac{(2 n-2 s)!}{2^{n-s} n!(n-s)}$$\n$(+2)$\nand finally the trigonometrical expression for the surface har-\n",
